legacy.description:
Entities of the old AppDaemon/MQTT bridge **{client_id}** were found. The following {count} entities can be taken over by this integration. They keep their entity ID, so history, long-term statistics (✔), dashboards and automations continue:

| Old entity (MQTT) | New entity | Last value | Statistics |
|---|---|---|---|
{table}

Not transferable (removed, history stays in the database): {skipped}

**Stop the AppDaemon app / getjudo service before you continue.** The old MQTT entities and their device are removed.

statistics.description:
Long-term statistics (incl. **costs** of the energy dashboard) of the old AppDaemon/MQTT bridge were found under other entity IDs. They are copied into the entities of this integration (only hours before their own data), sums are continued, so the energy dashboard shows one continuous series:

| Old statistic | New statistic | Period | Hours copied |
|---|---|---|---|
{table}

Energy dashboard is switched to the new entities:
{energy}

Left over entities removed (history stays in the database): {remove}

Create a backup first. The old statistics are kept unless you choose to delete them.

